 "drivingQuestion": "What is R' Eliezer ben Yaakov's statement alluded to by the mishna?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Identified as his baraita teaching from Deut. 26:4.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "menachot.61a.15",
   "daf": "61a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "וְהַבִּכּוּרִים, כְּדִבְרֵי רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב. מַאי רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב? דְּתַנְיָא: ״וְלָקַח הַכֹּהֵן״, לִימֵּד עַל הַבִּכּוּרִים שֶׁטְּעוּנִין תְּנוּפָה, דִּבְרֵי רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «The first fruits» also require waving, «in accordance with the statement of Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov.» The Gemara asks: «What is» the statement of «Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov,» alluded to here? The Gemara answers that it is «as it is taught» in a baraita: The verse states with regard to the first fruits: «“And the priest shall take» the basket from your hand, and place it before the altar of the Lord your God” (Deuteronomy 26:4). This «taught» a halakha «concerning the first fruits, that they require waving;» this is «the statement of Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov.»"
  }
 ],
